tent maintenance without publishing repetitive SEO pages."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/identity.css"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/images/portfolio-icon-180.png"><link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest"></head><body data-page="content-strategy-and-search-intent.html" class="academy page-lesson master-refresh"><header class="academy-header" id="top"><a class="academy-brand personal-brand" href="/"><span>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Personal Digital Portfolio · MBK Global</small></span></a><button class="academy-menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="academy-nav">Menu <span>+</span></button><nav id="academy-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href='/about'>About</a><a href='/projects'>Projects</a><a href='/services'>Services</a><a class='header-cta' href='/hire-me'>Let’s talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><details class="portfolio-more"><summary>More</summary><div class="portfolio-panel"><section><h2>Professional work</h2><a href='/case-studies'>Case Studies</a><a href='/changelog'>Projects Changelog</a><a href='/delivered-project'>Process</a><a href='/resources'>Resources</a><a href='/news'>Notes</a></section><section><h2>Contact &amp; career</h2><a href='/book-a-call'>Book a Call</a><a href='/resume'>Resume / CV</a><a href='/hire-me'>Hire Me</a></section><section><h2>Content &amp; media</h2><a href='/gallery'>Gallery</a><a href='/blog'>Blog &amp; Articles</a><a href='/faq'>FAQs</a></section><section><h2>Personal brand</h2><a href='/about-muhammad-bakhtawar-khan'>Founder Profile</a><a href='/social'>Social Profiles</a><a href='/official-links'>Official Links</a></section></div></details><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch color theme">◐</button></nav></header>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
<main class="container academy-main" id="main-content"><section class="academy-page-hero"><div class="academy-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href='/blog'>Learning library</a></div><div class="academy-kicker">lesson <span> / MBK GLOBAL</span></div><h1>Content Strategy and Search Intent</h1><p>A sustainable content strategy starts with real audience questions and the information you can reliably provide. Publishing fewer, more distinct pages is often more useful than scaling near-identical posts.</p></section><div class="academy-reading-layout"><aside class="academy-toc"><p class="academy-kicker">IN THIS GUIDE</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#section-1"><span>01</span>Build a topic inventory</a><a href="#section-2"><span>02</span>Map intent to a page type</a><a href="#section-3"><span>03</span>Create a useful brief</a><a href="#section-4"><span>04</span>Write with evidence and clarity</a><a href="#section-5"><span>05</span>Maintain and consolidate carefully</a></nav><div class="academy-author"><img src="/assets/images/mbk-personal-favicon-96.png" width="38" height="38" alt=""><div>Bakhtawar Khan<small>Founder, MBK Global</small></div></div><p class="academy-read-note">2 min read · Practical learning notes<br>Learn. Apply. Make it your own.</p><a class='academy-text-link' href='/resources'>More learning resources ↗</a></aside><div class="academy-reading-body"><article class="content-page"><header><p class="eyebrow">MBK Global · Practical guide</p></header><section><h2 id="section-1">Build a topic inventory</h2><p>List the pages you already have, their primary audience, purpose, supporting evidence and internal links. Identify overlap before drafting anything new. A page that serves a distinct task may deserve to remain separate even when it shares vocabulary with another page.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-2">Map intent to a page type</h2><p>People may want to learn a concept, compare options, complete a task or evaluate a service. Match the page format to that need: a checklist for implementation, a guide for learning, a project page for demonstrated work, and a contact page for enquiries.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-3">Create a useful brief</h2><p>State the intended reader, question, key points, facts that need verification, examples available, related internal pages and what the page should help the reader do next. Identify evidence gaps instead of filling them with assumptions.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-4">Write with evidence and clarity</h2><p>Use plain language, explain unfamiliar terms and provide concrete steps or examples. Separate verified experience from general advice. Do not invent client results, testimonials, qualifications, publication dates or statistics.</p></section><section><h2 id="section-5">Maintain and consolidate carefully</h2><p>Review pages for accuracy, outdated links and overlap. If consolidating URLs, choose the closest relevant destination, transfer genuinely useful information, update internal links and test redirects. Review Search Console data before irreversible removals when available.</p></section>
<p><strong>About this guide:</strong> This is general educational guidance. Adapt recommendations to your site's actual stack, risk and audience, and verify changes before publishing.</p>
<p>Explore related work: <a href='/web-development'>web development</a>, <a href='/projects'>projects</a>, and <a href='/contact'>contact</a>.</p></article></div></div><div data-portrait-track data-caption="A personal archive / Bakhtawar Khan"></div></main>
